  "query_id": "1065",
  "title_query": "I am a parent of two teenage daughters, and they both keep asking me to purchase a Labubu. I don’t understand their crush on the toy, and I am willing to do some research and find out more information about “The Labubu Phenomenon” to be on the same wave with my kids.\nLabubu, a character and brand of collectible plush toy monster elves created by Hong Kong designer Kasing Lung and marketed by Pop Mart, a Chinese toy company, has gained significant popularity, with fans lining up to purchase them and even celebrities like Rihanna being spotted with them. I need a report on “The Labubu Phenomenon” that has led to a surge in global revenue for Pop Mart, with the company's founder becoming significantly wealthier. The report should contain the explanation why these figurines have become viral sensations, particularly on platforms like TikTok.",
